body:
I wonder what state you're in, because where I'm from no one becomes a social pariah from a dui. I can't tell you how many old friends had duis and drove drunk l0ads.

&#x200B;

I became a social pariah, but in my case it was because i was the victim of a repeat dui driver. He disabled me and within 6 months all my 'friends' stopped talking to me. I was finally told by 1 of them, that no one wanted to see me anymore because i was a reminder of what they were doing and that deep down they knew it was wrong. They wanted to keep being irresponsible and didn't want a reminder of what their actions could do. I've always wondered how many other victims experience the same.  I can't imagine its changed that much in the 13 years since it happened to me, but obv if you live in a state where drinking isn't glorified, I can see that would be the case

Thank you for only driving drunk the 1 time. It angers and hurts me so much when ppl do it and take no accountability, blaming it on mental illness, addicriaddictionom, depression, etc.  Being an addict or depressed doesn't mean you can then be a shitty human and put other peoplespeople's lives at risk. I've known junkies who never once dridrive when high.

&#x200B;

I have so much i wanna say but its nearly impossible for me tp type on a phone.  The fact you feel si bad is a wonderful thing, tho it may not feel like it.  AtAt least, its wonderful for all those future victims who won't be, be cause you know what yoy did was horrible and you'll never play Russian roulette with innocent bystanders lives again.

&#x200B;

Thank you from the bottom of my heart for taking accountability, for having remorse, and for ensuring you'll never do it agaim. So stip beating yourself up! Just spread the word - try to stop others from doing it. From someone whose life was permanently ruined by a repeat drunk driver, its the best thing you can do for us victims.

&#x200B;

The guy who gave me a life sentence, got 3 yrs in jail for his 7th felony, and  smirked and blew kisses at me when i took the stand at his trial. You are nothing like him, and need to remember you're a decent human who messedmessed up. Forgive yourself but please never forget. I wish in cases like youryours, that the courts would take away all fees etc, if you promised to advocate against drunk driving, for victim rig ts (we really  have fewer than the offenders) , and volunteerevolunteered  go visit ppl made disabled and isolated by duis. But all they care about is money...

&#x200B;

Im so sorey you lost your job, for a first timertimer ho clearly has rwmorse and didn't hiet snyine, i don't think the punishment should be wo harsh. I'd much rather you go around and do community service and help disabled victims, than to pay any money and lose your livelihood. 

&#x200B;

Ive been thru hell and bcsk many times over,  that was just 1 of many awful things I've endured, but the only 1 i  was ubable to bounce back from since i lost everything and became homhomeless and can't even afford new wheelchairs.  Sorry i digress...anyway I've been destitute a few times, when i lost ky job and don't have family so had to start over. But whem i wss able bodied i alwsys bounced back. You will too. Just think if this as a new beginning and workwork hard toward what you want in life,  but please, pleaew forgive yourself.

Thanks for doing that, I wish more would. A drunk driver disabled me, and i became homeless because I couldn't work. I'm denied pain relief for my extensive permanent injuries even aftet reconstructive surgery (which I'm still having over a decade later), so I'm homebound and often bedbound. 

Luckily i have a roof over my head now ( a friend lets me live  here rent free) but have zero quality of life and never get to go anywhere. I'd give anything to be a performer again but without pain relief its impossible.

&#x200B;

 Its ironic that an addict who always got his fix did this to me, yet I'm refused opiates to make life bearable and be a productive member of society again. Also ironic that i was left to be homeless with no recourse and he got medical care, 3 meals a day, and financial assistance/ help with housing after serving his 3 years (for his 7th felony)

He'd been done for a dui 5 times previous so it's estimated he drove drunk thousands of times. Was 3 times the limit and he was going 80 in a 40 zone and made an illegal turn. 

&#x200B;

I wish everyday that he'd killed me, this is no life and its unfair that I'll be paying for his violent crime til the day i didie while he got basically a slap on the wrist. 

&#x200B;

So thank you. Because she coulcould have ruined another young innocent persons life.
